        "passage": "Scrumban Hybrid Flow. When to use it. Scrumban combines the pull system and WIP limits of Kanban with selected Scrum practices such as regular retrospectives and lightweight planning. It suits small teams, often six people or fewer, who own a live product and must balance roadmap features with a moderate, steady stream of interrupts, typically fifteen to thirty five percent of capacity.",
